ADR-0047 rulings 1/5/6. Two community overlays move from docs/ -- which
pyproject.toml does not package, so an installed hypergumbo could not read
them and they shipped to nobody -- into
hypergumbo_core/io_primitives_overlays/. They declare `provenance: community`
and a dated `retrieved:`, and are selected PER LANGUAGE (INV-lufib: a
catalogue applied to every language once hard-failed any repo containing a
second one).

THE PERMISSION IS CONDITIONAL AND THE CONDITION IS THE STDERR LINE. A run
that loads community rows prints, per queried language, the file, its
retrieval date, where to override it and how to switch it off -- shaped after
the in_progress warning and wired at the same three consumers so it cannot
fire in one and be silent in another. catalog_provenance gains a
`shipped_default` key alongside: a THIRD state, because "hypergumbo shipped it
and does not vouch for it" is a value `user_supplied` cannot express, and
collapsing it into either neighbour re-opens the INV-zosun gap.

AN UNVOUCHED ROW ADDS FINDINGS AND NEVER LICENSES THE ALL-CLEAR. This is the
property the feature rests on. INV-buzab makes "the catalogue classified this
call" mean "this call was examined", and an examined call stops blocking a
clean verdict -- so shipping these rows unmarked would have turned "never
writes to the host filesystem" from inconclusive into CONFIRMED for every
repository using requests, on the strength of rows describing only its NETWORK
surface. That is INV-zubuh's "presence of SOME rows must not vouch for the
rest", arriving through a new door. Rows from a shipped default are stamped
`unvouched` AT MERGE (not read from the file, so a file cannot claim
otherwise) and a call they classify still counts as unexamined. Detection is
untouched: the egress is visible, and adding a sink only ever adds a finding.

A SHIPPED DEFAULT MAY NOT DECLARE module_completeness, refused at load rather
than reviewed at merge. That entry is the single grant of confirmability -- a
closed-world claim that an unmatched call into a module is an examined
negative -- and granting one by default hands every user a claim about their
own dependencies that they never made. hypergumbo-self.yaml therefore stays
under docs/: it is hypergumbo's own overlay for its own dependency set and
carries exactly those grants.

A DEFAULT DOES NOT RESTATE THE CATALOGUE'S STDLIB CLAIM. `merge` is
self-over-argument with the overlay as receiver, so without care python went
provenance_declared -> in_progress the moment defaults loaded and every python
run would have emitted "results may be incomplete" beside the true
disclosure. Community rows are outside the enumeration provenance_declared
asserts, so a default preserves base status and provenance; a USER overlay's
effect on status is left exactly as it was.

Also: --no-default-overlays on io-boundaries and verify-claims;
io_primitives_overlays registered in YAML_CATALOGS with no channel of its own
(a user's rows for this content belong in the io_primitives channel, and a
second home for one kind of edit is the drift the registry prevents).

